## Third-party material

Two different things, kept apart on purpose.

**Work this repository carries.** Some files here incorporate third-party work, adapted or in part. Where one does, a `NOTICE.md` sits beside that file naming the upstream, its author, and its license, and a copy of that license ships in `licenses/`. Those upstream terms govern their own portions; this license governs everything else, and governs the work as a whole to the extent the upstream terms allow. **Nothing in this license narrows a right an upstream license grants you in its own material.**

**Packages a tool installs on your machine.** Those are yours under their own licenses. This repository redistributes none of them, and each tool names what it will install.

## Your work is yours

A license covers the software. Anything you make with it belongs to you.

## The base plugin is separate

This plugin expects the Wiser plugin alongside it. Wiser ships under its own license, free for an individual, and nothing here changes that. Needing a license for this plugin does not mean you need one for Wiser.

